#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Live view of the sign's screen for the dashboard, with remote mouse and
keyboard. Started by signage-agent for a "stream" command; it relays the
WebRTC handshake between this process and the browser over the terminal's
WebSocket relay, and the video then goes straight to the browser.

  screen ─ ffmpeg (kmsgrab ─ VAAPI H.264) ─ pipe ─ GStreamer webrtcbin ═ browser
  browser ─ data channel "input" ─ uinput tablet and keyboard ─ cage

Talks to the agent in JSON lines:
  argv[1]  {"ice_servers": [...], "quality": "native"|"1080"|"720",
            "output": "DP-1"|"", "control": true, "bitrate": 0}
  stdout   {"t":"offer","sdp":...}  {"t":"info",...}  {"t":"error","message":...}
  stdin    {"t":"answer","sdp":...}  {"t":"stop"}

SIGNAGE_STREAM_SOURCE=test swaps the screen for ffmpeg's test pattern
(software x264), for testing without a GPU or a Wayland session.
"""

